          "filename": "OxHillParkKearnyStump.jpg",
          "caption": "Kearny's Stump at en:Ox Hill Battlefield Park, in Fairfax, Virginia, USA.  This was supposedly the location where en:Philip Kearny, a Union general, was killed during the en:Battle of Chantilly (or Ox Hill) during the Civil War.  He is now known to have died a short distance away, but the stump (replaced with this stone marker) is part of the survey definition for a memorial plot nearby.",
